#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ai-deploy-target — guided setup for a Debian/Ubuntu or Rocky Linux deploy target.

Run as root ON the target machine (the machine the forced-command gateway deploys to):

    sudo ./ai-deploy-target bootstrap
    sudo ./ai-deploy-target app add my-app
    sudo ./ai-deploy-target app list
    sudo ./ai-deploy-target ai-ops enable --key "ssh-ed25519 …" --from 203.0.113.5
    sudo ./ai-deploy-target ai-ops disable
    sudo ./ai-deploy-target doctor
    ./ai-deploy-target --version

Every command is interactive by default (prompts show a [default]); --yes accepts the
defaults (and fails when a required answer has no default and no flag). --check prints
the plan and changes nothing, but still validates the inputs.

Test mode
---------
`--root DIR` (with the environment variable AI_DEPLOY_TARGET_TEST=1) prefixes every
file path with DIR and resolves every system command from PATH, so tests can drop fake
scripts there. It never touches the real system. `chown`/`useradd` are just as fake as
everything else.

Real mode
---------
System commands are looked up once with shutil.which and a clear error (plus the apt/dnf
install command) is reported when a required command is missing.
"""

